# REQ-005: File Format Support & Conversion

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** None — pre-built ✅
**Risk:** Low (existing component); Medium (RTF conversion quality — known issue)
**Depends On:** REQ-004 (Document Viewer & Navigation)

> ⚠️ **Implementation note:** File format support and conversion is already built as a reusable component. **Do not re-implement.** V1b/V1c/V1d agents should reference and integrate the existing component. Confirm supported format list, conversion pipeline interface, and known RTF issue workarounds with the owning team before V1b.

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator or clinician,
I need documents in any supported format to be rendered consistently in the viewer,
So that I can read all inbound documents regardless of how they were created or transmitted.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] The following inbound formats are supported: PDF, TIFF, JPEG, PNG, Word (.doc/.docx), RTF, CDA XML.
- [ ] All formats except CDA XML are converted to PDF on ingestion and displayed via the PDF viewer (REQ-004).
- [ ] CDA XML documents are rendered using an XSL stylesheet to produce a structured, human-readable view.
- [ ] Where an RTF document fails to convert to PDF due to source file format issues, an explicit error is surfaced to the user (rather than silently failing or displaying a blank document).
- [ ] The original source file is preserved alongside the converted rendition and is available for export in its original format (see REQ-006).

---

## Known Issue: RTF Conversion

> RTF → PDF conversion has known failures caused by source file format quality issues (malformed or non-standard RTF). This is a pre-existing limitation of the reusable component. The requirement captures the expected failure behaviour; resolution of the underlying conversion issue is tracked separately by the owning team.

