## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-010:** Error Handling Patient Safety — conversion failures must surface explicit errors; never render a blank or partial document silently
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — original file preserved so content is recoverable even if rendition fails

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-014:** Conversion failure results in blank or unreadable document displayed — clinician believes document has no content
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low–Medium (higher for RTF)
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-015:** CDA XML stylesheet rendering omits or misrepresents structured clinical content
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-016:** Original file lost after conversion — content unrecoverable if rendition is incorrect
  - **Severity:** Medium
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-013:** Explicit error state for conversion failures; never silent blank render
  - **Type:** Error Handling
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete (for awareness; does not recover content)

- **MIT-DOC-014:** Original source file preserved at rest alongside PDF rendition
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-015:** CDA XML stylesheet validated against known CDA document structures; rendering reviewed as part of clinical safety assessment
  - **Type:** Validation
  - **Effectiveness:** Partial (stylesheet coverage must be maintained as CDA profiles evolve)

