## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — original files and PDF renditions encrypted at rest (AES-256-GCM)
- **IG-010:** Retention Policy Enforcement — both original and rendition subject to NHS records retention schedules (IF3005)

### Data Handling
- Original source file retained alongside PDF rendition; both subject to the same retention and deletion schedule
- CDA XML stylesheet rendering does not write intermediate files to unencrypted storage
- Conversion pipeline processes documents in memory or encrypted temporary storage; no plaintext intermediate files persisted to disk

---

## Dimension 3: Security

### Applicable Guardrails
- **AUTH-004:** Authorization Required — document content (both original and rendition) accessible only to authorised users
- **SEC-001:** TLS Encryption — all document content served over TLS 1.2+

### Security Requirements
- Conversion pipeline sandboxed; malformed RTF or XML files must not be able to exploit the conversion process (e.g. XML external entity injection in CDA XML)
- CDA XML must be parsed with external entity resolution disabled (XXE prevention)
- XSL stylesheet is a controlled, versioned artefact — not user-supplied

---

## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance

### Product KPIs
- Conversion success rate per format
- Conversion latency (ingestion received → rendition available)
- RTF conversion failure rate (tracked separately given known issue)
- CDA XML stylesheet render success rate

### Observable Events (OTEL Instrumentation)
- `documents.conversion.initiated` — conversion triggered for an ingested document
- `documents.conversion.completed` — rendition successfully produced
- `documents.conversion.failed` — conversion failed; error type and source format recorded
- `documents.conversion.cda_rendered` — CDA XML stylesheet rendering completed

### Performance SLOs
- Conversion success rate: ≥ 99% for PDF, TIFF, JPEG, PNG, Word
- Conversion success rate: best-effort for RTF (known issue; tracked separately)
- Conversion latency: p95 < 30 seconds from ingestion to rendition available
- CDA stylesheet render: p95 < 5 seconds

### Alerting Conditions

| Condition | Threshold | Severity | Channel |
|---|---|---|---|
| Conversion failure rate spike | > 1% for any supported format (excluding RTF) | CRITICAL | On-call page |
| RTF conversion failure spike | > 10% of RTF conversions (known issue — tracked separately) | HIGH | Ops alert |
| Conversion latency breach | p95 > 30 seconds from ingestion to rendition | HIGH | Ops alert |
| CDA stylesheet render failure | > 0.5% of CDA documents fail stylesheet rendering | HIGH | Ops alert |

